#!zsh

## "Reloads" ZSH by replacing the current ZSH instance with a new one.
# This is primarily used to re-load dotfile config changes.
#
# This function does not do any normal ZSH cleanup procedures (writing history,
# .zlogout, zshexit, etc), because it `exec`s. This unexpected functionality
# is why it has a `!` in the name (modeled after Ruby's "mutating methods").
#
# To perform normal ZSH cleanup procedures, you have to append this function
# to `zshexit_functions` then exit normally. Unfortunately, due to a bug
# ZSH 5.9, this must be done in a top-level interactive call, so something like
# an alias is required:
#    alias reload='zshexit_functions+=reload!; exit'
##

# No arguments are supported.
if (( $# != 0 )) then
	print -ru2 "$0: no arguments are accepted"
fi

# Startup options to give to the new shell
local -a opts
if [[ -o LOGIN ]] opts+=-i
if [[ -o LOGIN ]] opts+=-l

# Run ZSH
exec =zsh $opts
